-- SRAL LIMS: seed the test catalog from the public site's 12 service categories (build/design-data.json),
-- so the LIMS and foodwatertesting.com never disagree about what SRAL tests for or under which standard.
-- Numeric bounds (permissible_limit_lo/hi) are parsed from the published limit text where it is a plain
-- number or range; where the published limit says "No relaxation", the published Acceptable limit for
-- that same parameter is used instead (both columns are already public on the parameter's category page).
-- Non-numeric limits (microbiology presence/absence, FSSAI label "basis" columns, etc.) are left null:
-- lims.enter_result() then leaves within_limit null rather than guessing, and a reviewer judges it.


-- sanity: every category from the public site is represented
do $$ declare v_n int; begin
  select count(distinct category_slug) into v_n from lims.test_catalog;
  if v_n <> 12 then raise exception 'expected 12 categories in the seed, found %', v_n; end if;
end $$;
